@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+`Flask.run` currently splits `SERVER_NAME` at its first colon. This prevents a
+bracketed IPv6 host and port from being used as the development server's
+defaults.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` values when deriving the default host and
+  port for `Flask.run`.
+- Keep existing hostname, explicit argument, and port-zero behavior unchanged.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `development-server-defaults`: Derive development-server defaults from
+  configured server names, including bracketed IPv6 literals.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/flask/app.py` development-server default selection.
+- `tests/test_basic.py` coverage for IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` defaults.
